<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Orange River Colony</h1><p class="st-meta">1902 CE – 1910 CE · capital Bloemfontein</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British colony that replaced the Orange Free State after the Second Boer War, until it joined the Union of South Africa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>British forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein">Bloemfontein</a> in March 1900, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> proclaimed the annexation of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/orange-free-state">Orange Free State</a> as the Orange River Colony in May 1900. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> commandos fought on until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-vereeniging">Treaty of Vereeniging</a> in May 1902, when British rule became effective.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>During the war, farms were burned and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> women and children held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a>, where thousands died, as did many black Africans in separate camps. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-milner">Lord Milner's</a> reconstruction the colony was run by appointed officials. After the Liberal victory in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, responsible government was granted in 1907, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orangia-unie">Orangia Unie</a> party under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-fischer">Abraham Fischer</a> took office.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1910 the colony joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/union-of-south-africa">Union of South Africa</a> as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-free-state-province">Orange Free State Province</a>, keeping <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein">Bloemfontein</a> as the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appellate-division-of-the-supreme-court-of-south-africa">Appellate Division</a>, which made it the country's judicial capital.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/orange-river-colony.jpg" alt="Orange River Colony" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Philip Ronan · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Orange_River_Colony.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1902 CE – 1910 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bloemfontein</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alfred Milner, Abraham Fischer</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch, Afrikaans, Sesotho, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1906&amp;focus=orange-river-colony" aria-label="Orange River Colony on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5364 3242 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Orange River Colony lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5684 3498L5684 3498M5684 3498L4997 651M5684 3498L5746 3380"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5684 3498h0M4997 651h0M5746 3380h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5684 3498h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5684 3498h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bloemfontein. <a href="/atlas?year=1906&amp;focus=orange-river-colony">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
